  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2314216386f93e848b802d3e5aa8e609, type: 3}
  m_Name: Acute Gastroenteritis
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MedicalCase
  title: Acute Gastroenteritis (Acute Diarrhea)
  type: Common
  category: Infectious
  description: Defined as three or more loose or watery stools in a 24-hour period,
    lasting less than 14 days. Rotavirus is the most common cause of acute diarrhea
    in the Philippines.
  symptoms: 'Watery diarrhea for several days.   Vomiting and abdominal pain.   Signs
    of severe dehydration: lethargy, sunken eyes, dry lips, slow skin pinch, decreased
    urine output, and refusal to drink.'
  pathology: Often caused by viral infections (like rotavirus) and exacerbated by
    structural risk factors like a lack of access to clean water.
  treatment: 'ral Rehydration Solution (ORS) is the cornerstone of therapy.   Zinc
    supplementation (20 mg daily for 10-14 days) is strongly recommended for children.  
    Severe dehydration requires hospital admission for immediate IV fluids.   Antibiotics
    are NOT routinely recommended for non-bloody diarrhea. '
  keyFeatures: Dehydration severity must be assessed clinically; lethargy, sunken
    eyes, and a slow skin pinch are critical signs of severe dehydration requiring
    admission.
  requiredStageLevel: 1
